Z||000000||WKDFIRO||09-11-2001||09:09 PM||||I was heading to work one morning and as I was winding down the hill I heard the engine give two odd cluncks and I felt car shudder. Everything seemed okay until I got onto the freeway when I realized that my speedometer wasn't working. Crap I thought, time to find out if the little GM gremlin I heard about exists. <P>It does.<P>If you didn't know, GM put a little trick in the ECM so that if the speedo stops working (or is unplugged to prevent adding miles to the gauge) it will prevent the engine from idling. It will run fine but just won't idle. <P>When I took out the speed sensor I found that it had broken from the rod coming out of the sensor. Ive gotten a new speed sensor but it didn't come with the gear! The gear is not only seperate but is now discontinued!!!!<P>I figure I will head to the pick a part place soon for an old one but I figured that everyone should know! ||||reg||8
