Z||000003||mike tatara||09-12-2001||12:00 AM||||HAD THE SAME PROBLEM WHEN  DOING MY CONVERSION THE STUPID PLASTIC GEAR FALLS OFF AND LAYS INSIDE THE TRANNY<P>I DONT HAVE THE HEART TO TELL YOU WHAT THAT INVOLVES    SPLITTING THE TRANNY CASE IN HALF   COMES TO MIND||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||09-12-2001||12:17 PM||||Maybe I misunderstood what you said. I took it to mean that Delphi wrote the code so a VSS error will intentionally distrupt the idle. I've seen nothing like that. <P>Now getting to idle from higher R's without the VSS and (therefore no DFCO/stall saver) is a bit tricky since the ECM won't float the R's until the speed comes now. <P>But at a stop, the idle shouldn't be affected since the VSS is not operating anyway. There's no bit set to foul up the idle.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||09-13-2001||10:49 PM||||I hadn't tried it in the manner of which you speak but it does make sense that the input from the VSS would effect the "stall saver."  <P>If you come to a stop however, how would the engine stay running if it won't float the R's? Starting in the garage would not probably be effected but it can be a pain in the butt getting it back home if the engine won't stay running that well by itself without help! Simply disconnect your VSS and you will know exactly what Im going through. <P>I wish it was just the plactic gear, part of the metal stem apparently snapped. (Something Ive never seen) and as for trying to get it back, well I heard and felt it go through the gears when it came off and I don't think I want it back now! The magnet in the tranny case should hold on to the metal fragments until I go in for another clutch or any other reason to pull the tranny. <P>My real rant was the price of a new sensor and not coming with the gear!||||reg||6
Z||000006||GodSend||09-14-2001||12:26 AM||||Had a similar type problem only thankgod the car was parked... Actually I was just checking my tranny fluid.. popped off the wires, Undid that littel bolt, and swung that little metal retainer out the way... I yanked on the fitting for about 5 minutes and it FINALLY came out... except.. oups.. theres the red plastic gear in the tranny.. I fumbled around with my pinky for awhile and finally got it in an area where I could grab it the old trust needlenosers .... had me worried for awhlie though,, ||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||09-14-2001||04:36 PM||||No, I'm real familiar with both problems (dropping gear and no stall-saver). When you clutch it, the engine drops to idle RPM, overshoots and stalls. But if it doesn't die, it should smooth out and idle at 900. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||09-14-2001||04:44 PM||||Terry are you sure you know what you're talking about?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> j/k Seriously, my friend Ryan drove his car for a few weeks without the gear (after dropping it in and not knowing it until it was long gone) and he didn't have any problems with the way the car ran.||||reg||1
